{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/4azhjm","slide":3,"text":"Explain why the project uses each interface style. Topics carry streams, services handle short requests, and actions retain state for long-running work. DDS matches endpoint names and types, while QoS controls reliability, durability, queue depth, deadline and lifespan. Status messages also carry boot IDs, sequences and validity so consumers can reject stale evidence.\n\nSources:\n- src/amr_interfaces\n- src/amr_interfaces/include/amr_interfaces/qos_profiles.hpp\n- src/amr_bringup/config/interface_ownership.yaml"}
