{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/titx66","slide":4,"text":"Gazebo publishes native simulation endpoints. ros_gz_bridge converts them into ROS 2 messages. The project adapters then create stable names under /amr so downstream nodes do not depend on the simulator's native names. RViz2 subscribes to graph data for inspection and has no accepted velocity authority.\n\nSources:\n- src/amr_simulation/launch/amr_simulation.launch.py\n- src/amr_simulation/rviz/sensors.rviz\n- src/amr_sensor_adapters\n- src/amr_factory/launch/factory_localization.launch.py"}
